{
  "title": "Telecom MCP tools",
  "uid": "telecom-mcp-tools",
  "tags": [
    "telecom",
    "mcp",
    "generated"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "description": "Generated by scripts/generate_observability.py from the KPI and SLO catalogues. Edit those, not this file.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Tool calls",
      "description": "How much work is this thing doing?\n\nThe denominator for every ratio below. A sudden fall is an outage upstream of us and is worth more attention than a rise.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=~\"ok|deduplicated|failed|denied|guardrail_blocked\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Tool calls",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Success ratio",
      "description": "Are calls working?\n\nSuccessful and deduplicated calls over all calls. Deduplicated counts as success because the caller got the answer they asked for.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.995
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "(sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=\"ok\"}[5m])) + sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=\"deduplicated\"}[5m]))) / clamp_min(sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=~\"ok|deduplicated|failed|denied|guardrail_blocked\"}[5m])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Success ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Failure ratio",
      "description": "Are we breaking?\n\nCalls that were authorized and then failed. This is our fault or the middleware's; a denial or a guardrail block is not counted here, because a control working correctly is not an error.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=\"failed\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=~\"ok|deduplicated|failed|denied|guardrail_blocked\"}[5m])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Failure ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency p95",
      "description": "Is it fast enough for a live call?\n\nA voice case has a five minute budget and an agent may need several tools inside it. p95 is the number that decides whether that is possible.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 2.0
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(tool_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "Latency p95",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Latency p99",
      "description": "How bad is the tail?\n\nThe customer who is already annoyed is in this bucket. Track it separately from p95: a p95 that holds while p99 doubles is a retry storm.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 8.0
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(tool_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "Latency p99",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Calls over the time budget",
      "description": "How many calls blew the ten second budget?\n\nObservations above the last histogram bucket. A quantile hides these; a count does not, and this is the one number that maps to a real customer sitting in silence.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(tool_duration_seconds_count[5m])) - sum(increase(tool_duration_seconds_bucket{le=\"10\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Calls over the time budget",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Load shed ratio",
      "description": "Are we refusing work because we are full?\n\nShedding is the designed behaviour under load, not a bug, but a non-zero value means capacity is the constraint and the next step is replicas.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.01
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=\"shed\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=~\"ok|deduplicated|failed|denied|guardrail_blocked\"}[5m])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Load shed ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Deduplication ratio",
      "description": "How often is a caller repeating itself?\n\nA small number is the idempotency store doing its job. A large one is an agent retrying because it thinks we failed, which is a latency problem wearing a different hat.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=\"deduplicated\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=~\"ok|deduplicated|failed|denied|guardrail_blocked\"}[5m])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Deduplication ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backend retry ratio",
      "description": "Is the middleware healthy?\n\nAttempts beyond the first, over all attempts. Rises before failures do, which makes it the earliest honest warning we have.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(backend_attempts_total{stage!=\"1\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(backend_attempts_total[5m])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Backend retry ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Authorization denial ratio",
      "description": "How much is the kernel refusing?\n\nA steady low number is normal: agents probe tools they do not hold scopes for. A step change means a token, a role or a claim namespace changed, and it will usually have changed by accident.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=\"denied\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=~\"ok|deduplicated|failed|denied|guardrail_blocked\"}[5m])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Authorization denial ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Guardrail block ratio",
      "description": "What are the guardrails stopping?\n\nNear zero is expected and is not a reason to relax anything. A spike in the injection stage is an attack or a bad prompt template; a spike in argument_size is usually a client bug.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 24
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(guardrail_decisions_total[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(tool_calls_total{outcome=~\"ok|deduplicated|failed|denied|guardrail_blocked\"}[5m])), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "Guardrail block ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Output guardrail blocks",
      "description": "Did we nearly hand a secret to the model?\n\nThis should be zero forever. Any non-zero value means a write happened and the response was withheld, and it is a page rather than a ticket: redaction has met a field it does not know about.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 24
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(guardrail_decisions_total{stage=~\"output_.*\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Output guardrail blocks",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Tickets created",
      "description": "What did the agent actually do for people?\n\nUp is not automatically good. Read it beside the callback and refund numbers: more tickets and fewer callbacks is the agent resolving things.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(tool_calls_total{tool=\"create_support_ticket\",outcome=\"ok\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Tickets created",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Callbacks scheduled",
      "description": "How often does this end with a human ringing back?\n\nThe closest thing to a containment measure we have. A rise means the agent is handing more away, which may be correct and is never neutral.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(tool_calls_total{tool=\"schedule_callback\",outcome=\"ok\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Callbacks scheduled",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Refund approvals requested",
      "description": "How much money is queued behind a supervisor?\n\nNothing has moved when this increments; it is a queue depth for humans. Watch it against the action budget: a rise in both is one case looping.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 32
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(tool_calls_total{tool=\"request_refund_approval\",outcome=\"ok\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "Refund approvals requested",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
